MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Carole King and Bread feel like natural next choices because I currently want warm vocals and gentle, melodic songwriting, which connect with my Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie listening.",
    "The Beach Boys' vocal harmonies and sixties melodies fit my Beatles and AM Gold listening, while Fleetwood Mac offers the melodic rock and familiar-song collections I often choose."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Huey Lewis and Journey share an older pop-rock connection with some of my listening, but their upbeat or arena-rock sound feels less appealing than softer, song-focused music right now.",
    "Queen, the Rolling Stones, Elvis, and Bowie have connections to my interests, but that familiarity alone does not make them my first choices today; Bread and Carole King better match the mood I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My classic rock listening seems to have been taken as a broad desire for classic rock, when the particular sound and energy matter more to my choices today.",
    "I often choose greatest-hits collections, but the collection format alone does not make an artist appealing; I still need the songs to match my current listening mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie listening points toward the warm voices and gentler songwriting that make Carole King my strongest choice here.",
    "The harmonies and sixties melodies connected to my Beatles and AM Gold listening matter more today than a general connection to older rock hits."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in older music and compilations, but only some captured the gentle melodies, warm vocals, and harmonies I want right now."
}
